I did the following; I believe you'll understand what I've done; if not, ask
again.


library(statnet)
ideias = network.initialize(24)
comp1 = network.initialize(24)
comp2 = network.initialize(24)
nodes = read.csv('NODredeR.csv',header=T)
links = read.csv('LINredeR.csv',header=T)
set.vertex.attribute(ideias,"SEXO",nodes[,c(2)])
set.vertex.attribute(ideias,"IDADE",nodes[,c(3)])
set.vertex.attribute(ideias,"LOTA",nodes[,c(4)])
set.vertex.attribute(ideias,"TDIV",nodes[,c(5)])
set.vertex.attribute(ideias,"TEMP",nodes[,c(6)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp1,"SEXO",nodes[,c(2)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp1,"IDADE",nodes[,c(3)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp1,"LOTA",nodes[,c(4)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp1,"TDIV",nodes[,c(5)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp1,"TEMP",nodes[,c(6)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp2,"SEXO",nodes[,c(2)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp2,"IDADE",nodes[,c(3)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp2,"LOTA",nodes[,c(4)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp2,"TDIV",nodes[,c(5)])
set.vertex.attribute(comp2,"TEMP",nodes[,c(6)])
network.edgelist(links[links[3]==1,c(1,2)],ideias,names.eval="IDEIA")
set.edge.attribute(ideias,"IDEIA",1:138)
network.edgelist(links[links[4]==1,c(1,2)],comp1,names.eval="COMP1")
set.edge.attribute(comp1,"COMP1",1:124)
network.edgelist(links[links[5]==1,c(1,2)],comp2,names.eval="COMP2")
set.edge.attribute(comp1,"COMP2",1:45)


Hope this help.

Best regards,


