From handcock at stat.washington.edu  Mon Mar 23 10:55:18 2009
From: handcock at stat.washington.edu (Mark S. Handcock)
Date: Mon Mar 23 10:55:18 2009
Subject: [statnet_help] ERGM constraints for DAGs?
In-Reply-To: <Pine.WNT.4.64.0903230824020.3188@vinaya.csde.washington.edu>
Message-ID: <C5ED1B16.1FFEE%handcock@stat.washington.edu>

Hi Simon,

The current "constraints" is very flexible and powerful but does not have
DAGs explicitly coded in. However it would be possible to achieve using the
"offset" function on the "cycles" term. By setting the coefficients of these
to a large negative number, the graph space will be constrained to DAGs.

I hope this helps.

Mark

