Subject: [statnet_help] Multiple edges plot
In-Reply-To: <1238092734.6194.41.camel@jeroyadri-laptop>
References: <1238092734.6194.41.camel@jeroyadri-laptop>
Message-ID: <49D073C1.7080201@uci.edu>

Jeronimo Carballo wrote:
> Hello list,
> 
> I am a newbie in statnet and I need to plot a network with multiple
> (more than 2) edges between vertices. It is possible with statnet?
> 
>

Not with the native plot method.  One workaround is to encode multiplex 
information as an edge property (in a non-multiplex network), and plot 
that.  Alternately, you may want to create a custom display method.  (If 
you come up with an approach which yields good results, I'd be 
interested in seeing it -- in the long run, it would be nice to have 
intelligent default behavior for the standard plot method.)

-Carter

