Just to add to what Steve says:

The 'coef' function is really an R function, and the ergm version is  
called 'coef.ergm'.  I believe that coef.ergm does for an ergm what  
coef does for an lm -- that is, provide only the coefficients.  This  
seems the logical way to write coef.ergm to me (i.e., to do exactly  
what coef does in other non-ergm instances).  So when you say "that I  
should receive", I'm not sure I'd say that's the case.

Dave


