From handcock at stat.washington.edu  Mon Aug 24 10:53:03 2009
From: handcock at stat.washington.edu (Mark S. Handcock)
Date: Mon Aug 24 10:53:03 2009
Subject: [statnet_help] coef(ergm(Network ~ edges + triangles) )?
In-Reply-To: <alpine.WNT.1.10.0908241034050.736@stevegT400.csde.washington.edu>
Message-ID: <C6B8218F.24289%handcock@stat.washington.edu>

Hi Randall,

If you use:

sumfit <- summary(ergm(Network ~ edges + triangles) )

then sumfit will be a list with all the "subfields" (as components) in it.
Then, e.g.

sumfit

will print the usual summary you want and you can see the components via,
e.g., 

> names(sumfit)
 [1] "formula"          "randomeffects"    "digits"           "correlation"
 [5] "degeneracy.value" "offset"           "drop"             "covariance"
 [9] "pseudolikelihood" "independence"     "iterations"       "samplesize"
[13] "message"          "devtable"         "aic"              "bic"
[17] "coefs"            "asycov"           "asyse"

Cheers,

Mark
for the statnet team.

