From samstewart11 at gmail.com  Tue Dec 15 05:04:16 2009
From: samstewart11 at gmail.com (Sam Stewart)
Date: Tue Dec 15 05:04:16 2009
Subject: [statnet_help] Valued networks in network package
In-Reply-To: <6859125B-DE0F-4167-9A8A-6D58D660D1B1@reed.edu>
References: <6859125B-DE0F-4167-9A8A-6D58D660D1B1@reed.edu>
Message-ID: <5daac4820912150504v470628f1u991aeb3c40ecc062@mail.gmail.com>

You want to use the network.adjacency option to create a valued adjacency matrix

m = matrix(c(0,2,2,0),nrow=2)
n = network(m)
degree(n)
network.adjacency(m,n)
degree(n)
degree(m)

If you're familiar with R you'll a little confused by the syntax for
network.adjacency, where m is the adjacency matrix that defines the
values of the ties in n. The function (I think) takes care of the
assignment itself.

Hope that helps,
Sam Stewart

